# Normalise every text file to LF *in the repository*.
#
# THIS IS LOAD-BEARING, NOT TIDINESS. The pages are generated, and they are
# generated on two different platforms: by hand on Windows, where Python's
# `write_text` emits CRLF, and by the weekly GitHub Action on ubuntu-latest, where
# it emits LF. Without this file the repo stores whatever the last writer used, so
# the Action's "did anything actually change?" check —
#
#     git diff --quiet -- build/google-reviews.json site/
#
# — sees all 54 files in site/ as modified on EVERY run, purely from line endings.
# It would then commit and deploy a "refresh Google reviews" every week whether or
# not a single review changed, and a real change would be invisible in a diff that
# rewrites every line of every page.
#
# `text=auto` normalises on commit and un-normalises on checkout, so Windows still
# gets CRLF in the working tree and `git status` stays clean on both platforms.
# Verified: the staged blobs contain no CR bytes.
* text=auto

# Binary, so git must never touch these. `text=auto` does detect binary content on
# its own, but a webp or a woff2 that got line-ending translation applied to it is
# corrupt in a way that only shows up in a browser, so it is worth being explicit.
*.webp   binary
*.png    binary
*.ico    binary
*.woff2  binary
*.pdf    binary
*.heic   binary
